chapter ★ | The three-day plan: level 22, stretch 25 | Launch Wednesday to Friday, about 12 hours a day
id plan
type reference
> Level 22 by Friday night is the target and 25 is a bonus. Either leaves plenty of room
> for optional quests, every dungeon on the way and time spent at camp. If you're ahead,
> slow down and do the side chains; if you're behind, the soft profession targets give way
> first.
n Day 1 (launch day): Valley of Trials through the level 10 Orgrimmar stop and into the Crossroads
  detail Aim for 11 to 13, with Fishing 20 and the Fish Bowl, Enchanting 20 and the Enchanted Lute, and the Basic Campfire.
  detail After that, the day is about leveling.
n Day 2: the Crossroads loops, Thunder Bluff, Ratchet, Ragefire Chasm and the northern Barrens
  detail Day 2: the Crossroads loops, the Thunder Bluff run, Ratchet, Ragefire Chasm and the northern Barrens.
  detail Aim for 17 to 19. The Thunder Bluff run adds about 30 to 45 minutes of travel.
n Day 3: Undercity run through to Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon; level 22 is the target
  detail Day 3: the Undercity run with Ruins of Lordaeron, the oases and Camp Taurajo, the Succubus, Wailing Caverns, then Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon.
  detail Level 22 is the target; 25 with Expert Enchanting trained is the stretch.
  detail The Undercity run is another 30 to 45 minutes of zeppelins and walking, so budget for it.
n Ahead of schedule? The optional quests are worth it for the world
  detail Zalazane on the Echo Isles, Verog the Dervish, Hezrul Bloodmark, Wenikee's chain and the Northwatch escort.
n Launch crowds: when quest mobs are heavily contested, group with whoever else is waiting
  detail Shared kills beat standing in line.
n Log off in an inn or a city each night for rested XP
  detail So you start the next day with rested XP.

gate Flight paths unlocked by level 25
