  check Ratchet
  check Camp Taurajo
  check Thunder Bluff
  check Undercity
  check The Sepulcher (optional)
  check Sun Rock Retreat

chapter P | Profession leveling at a glance | Reference for the whole route
id prof
type reference
> The camp buffs come first and are covered in the chapters. This is the leveling path
> behind them, so you know what to craft whenever you're standing in a city with materials.
n Enchanting 1 to 25: {Enchant Bracer – Inferior Stamina} on your own bracers
  detail 1 Mote of Magic each. Orange to 15 and grey at 25.
  detail If you have spare Simple Wood (about 40c each), {Novice's Practice Wand} also gives skill until it greys at 15, but bracers alone get you there cheaper.
n Enchanting 10: {Lesser Magic Wand}, a real upgrade over the practice wand
  detail 1 Simple Wood, 1 Lesser Magic Essence; level 5, about 11 DPS. Craft it once you have an essence.
n Enchanting 15 to 90: {Enchant Chest – Inferior Stamina}, yellow at 70
  detail 1 Strange Dust each, 50c to learn at 15. Strange Dust comes from disenchanting greens.
n Enchanting 70: {Greater Magic Wand}, your best wand until the mid-teens
  detail 1 Simple Wood, 2 Lesser Magic Essence; level 13, about 17.5 DPS.
n Enchanting 90 to 130: {Enchant Cloak – Minor Protection}, yellow at 110
  detail 2s to learn at 70. Expert Enchanting at 125 from {Hgarth} in Sun Rock Retreat.
n Tailoring 1 to 44: {Bolt of Linen Cloth}, then {Linen Belt} carries 44 to 55
  detail Bolt of Linen Cloth is orange to 25 and green to 37. Linen Belt is learned at 15.
n Tailoring 55 to 100: {Bolt of Woolen Cloth}, then {Woolen Cape} from 81 to 100
  detail Bolt of Woolen Cloth from around 55, orange to 70.
n Tailoring 100 to 140: {Bolt of Silk Cloth}, {Stylish Red Shirt}, {Azure Silk Hood}, Expert
  detail Bolt of Silk Cloth: only the first 25 or so give skill, but you'll need about 175 bolts.
  detail Stylish Red Shirt 118 to 120, Azure Silk Hood 120 to 135, then Expert from {Josef Gregorian} in Undercity and {Formal White Shirt} 135 to 140.
n Fishing and Cooking: 20 for the Fish Bowl and the Basic Campfire on launch day
  detail The rest happens in the KubeCon week plan.
n Recipes worth buying: the Shadow set from {Jim'bek} at the Crossroads, 30 Favor each
  detail It's the Affliction Warlock set: Shadow Boots (Tailoring 60, wearable at 17), Shadow Gloves (75, wearable at 15), Shadow Sash (85, wearable at 12), Shadow Circlet (100, wearable at 20; the best piece at 20), Shadow Gown (110) and Shadow Leggings (125).
  detail Buy them as your Tailoring reaches each one.
n Enchanting recipes worth noting: Greater Magic Wand, Lesser Strength bracers, Soulstaff
  detail Greater Magic Wand at 70 (trainer; 2 Lesser Magic Essence and 1 Simple Wood).
  detail {Formula: Enchant Bracer – Lesser Strength} from {Kulwia} at Sun Rock Retreat for the next skill bracket.
  detail After 25, {Beneris} sells {Soulstaff} and {Orb of Souls} at Enchanting 140 for 45 Favor each.
n Disenchanting materials: no quest on this route rewards them, so disenchant greens
  detail No quest on this route rewards dust or essences directly, so it's all disenchanting.
  detail Greens up to item level 15 give Lesser Magic Essence (keep them: the Greater Magic Wand eats two per craft), and greens from item level 5 to 25 give Strange Dust.
  detail Reliable sources: Bloodtalon Matriarch's Raptorscale Pants (a green you can't wear), and every dungeon run: Ragefire, Ruins of Lordaeron and Wailing Caverns.
n Keep any {Craftsman's Writs} that ask for something you can make
  detail They drop from monsters as Sealed Craftsman's Writs.
  detail Azure Silk Hood (Tailoring 130) goes to the {Cowardly Peon} in Ashenvale for camp reputation and a pouch of silver.
n Camp objects to pick up: Fish Bowl, Enchanted Lute, Faction Banner, Spinning Wheel
  detail Fish Bowl (Fishing 20), Enchanted Lute (Enchanting 20), Faction Banner (Tailoring 20), Spinning Wheel (Tailoring 140).

chapter 1 | Valley of Trials | Levels 1-5
id ch1
> No profession trainers here, so this chapter is about stockpiling. Everything you loot
> now becomes skill points in the next two hours.
zone Durotar
q Speak to {Kaltunk} outside the Den, then {Gornek} inside: [Your Place In The World]
  done turnin [Your Place In The World]
q Take [Cutting Teeth] and [Wayward Weapons]
  done accept [Cutting Teeth], [Wayward Weapons]
q Kill 10 Mottled Boars outside the Den and pick up 6 abandoned training weapons
  detail Pick the weapons up off the ground in the same pass.
  done complete [Cutting Teeth], [Wayward Weapons]
q Head west to Hana'zua: [Sarkoth]. Kill him on the ledge above, turn in
  detail Then carry the follow-up back to {Gornek}.
  reward Sarkoth follow-up: Soft Wool Vest.
  done turnin [Sarkoth]
c Turn in [Cutting Teeth]. Take [Tainted Tablet] and hand it to {Nartok} in the Den
  reward Cutting Teeth: Soft Wool Boots.
  done turnin [Cutting Teeth], [Tainted Tablet]
q Pick up [Sting of the Scorpid], [Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise] and [Vile Familiars#792]
  verify Quest ID 792 for Zureetha's Vile Familiars is from Classic; check it on Forever
  detail Sting of the Scorpid from {Gornek}, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise from {Galgar}, and Zureetha's Vile Familiars from {Zureetha}.
  done accept [Sting of the Scorpid], [Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise], [Vile Familiars#792]
q Pick up [Lazy Peons] from {Foreman Thazz'ril}
  minlevel 3
  done accept [Lazy Peons]
c Take the Warlock [Vile Familiars#1499] from {Ruzan}: 6 Vile Familiar Heads
  verify Quest ID 1499 for the Warlock Vile Familiars is from Classic; check it on Forever
  done accept [Vile Familiars#1499]
q One loop: scorpid tails, 10 cactus apples, 5 sleeping peons, Vile Familiars; turn in
  detail Blackjack the 5 sleeping peons. The Vile Familiars are by the Burning Blade cave. Turn everything in.
  reward Sting of the Scorpid: Soft Wool Belt.
  reward Galgar: take the food (the profession books are for skills you aren't training).
  reward Zureetha's Vile Familiars: Primitive Hand Blade.
  done turnin [Sting of the Scorpid], [Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise], [Lazy Peons], [Vile Familiars#792]
c Return the heads to {Ruzan} and check that {Summon Imp} is in your spellbook
  detail Take Ruzan's message to {Zureetha}.
  reward Warlock Vile Familiars: Primitive Hand Blade again if offered; vendor the spare.
  done turnin [Vile Familiars#1499]
c Keep Imp training to a minimum: skip the demon trainer's Imp grimoires
  detail Skip the extra Firebolt ranks, Blood Pact and the rest.
  detail The Voidwalker takes over at level 10, so that coin is better spent on the Orgrimmar run and your own spells.
q Take [Thazz'ril's Pick] and [Burning Blade Medallion]
  done accept [Thazz'ril's Pick], [Burning Blade Medallion]
q In the cave, grab the pick and kill {Yarrog Baneshadow}
  done complete [Thazz'ril's Pick], [Burning Blade Medallion]
p Loot every {Linen Cloth} from the Burning Blade inside the cave
  detail The Burning Blade inside the cave are humanoids. Don't turn any of it into bandages.
q Turn in, accept [Report to Sen'jin Village], and grab [A Peon's Burden] from {Ukor}
  detail Ukor is on the road out.
  reward Burning Blade Medallion: whichever pants are cloth (Dust-covered Leggings or Ripped Pants, check the tooltip). Skip the Jagged Chain Vest.
  done turnin [Thazz'ril's Pick], [Burning Blade Medallion]
  done accept [Report to Sen'jin Village], [A Peon's Burden]

gate Leave the Valley with
  check Imp summoned and on your bar
  check 6-slot bag bought from the traveling gear stall (5s)
  check Every Linen Cloth you've looted
  check Every green still in your bags or on your character (each one is future Enchanting dust)

