  detail (most players find one to three by level 20), and the auction house sells them.
  detail Fill one line of what it asks for. Your first crate also gives a {Shipping Label} quest
  detail worth an extra 50 Merchant's Favor, once per character.
p Fill Fabrics crates with bolts, not raw cloth
  detail Crates of crafted goods pay double. An Apprentice Fabrics crate takes 20 Bolts of Linen for
  detail 10 Favor; a Journeyman one takes 6 Bolts of Woolen Cloth or 10 of silk for 20. With the
  detail Shipping Label bonus, your first crate covers two 30-Favor patterns.
p Spend Favor on Shadow patterns first at {Jim'bek} @49.6,29.5
  detail Favor shops at the camp: {Jim'bek} @49.6,29.5 sells Tailoring patterns, {Beneris} @49.6,29.8
  detail Enchanting formulas and {Aza'bek} @49.6,29.2 Cooking recipes. Shadow patterns first (see the
  detail profession plan); skip Venomous Smoothie and the other Cooking recipes for now.
